# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# QueryStream reproduction — .gitignore
#
# Three jobs, in order of importance:
#   1. never commit a credential
#   2. never commit benchmark video / dataset payloads
#   3. keep the repo reviewable — results summaries in, multi-GB raw traces out
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. SECRETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The judges read OPENAI_API_KEY from the environment only and never write it to
# disk (CLAUDE.md §13.7 decision 7). These patterns are belt-and-braces.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
env.sh
secrets.*
*secret*
*credential*
*_key
*_key.*
apikey*
api_key*
openai_key*
hf_token*
.netrc
.huggingface/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.aws/
.config/gcloud/

# ── 2. DATASETS & MEDIA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benchmark corpora live OUTSIDE this tree and must stay there:
#   StreamingBench  /iopsstor/scratch/cscs/dbartaula/eval_7_10_8_19/...  (246 GB)
#   OmniPro         /iopsstor/scratch/cscs/dbartaula/omnipro_data/       (1,262 videos)
#   OVO-Bench       chunked_videos/                                      (3,035 clips)
# These rules stop a copy or symlink from ever being staged.
/data/
datasets/
dataset/
videos/
chunked_videos/
*_data/
omnipro_data/
streamingbench/
questions_real.json
benchmark.json

# video / audio containers
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.avi
*.mov
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.flac
# ...except the 279 KB synthetic fixture test_integration.py builds against.
# (`/data/` above is anchored to the repo root precisely so tests/data/ survives:
#  git never descends into an excluded directory, so a negation inside one is dead.)
!tests/data/sample_bottle.mp4

# model weights & feature caches
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.tfrecord
hf_cache/
.cache/
checkpoints/

# ── 3. RUN ARTEFACTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately TRACKED, so a clone can reproduce every published number:
#   *raw_logs*.jsonl      per-frame R_t/D_t/T_t traces + raw_trigger_ts.
#                         CLAUDE.md §15.9/§15.10 re-derive the gate ablation and
#                         the debounce sweep from these, offline, with no GPU.
#   judge_*.jsonl         OpenAI judge requests + verdicts, so the OmniPro
#                         content scores (§19.2) re-score without re-paying.
#   summary.json / profile_summary.csv / figures/*.png / *_report.pdf
# Only genuinely regenerable scratch is ignored here.
slurm-*.out
*.sbatch.out
nohup.out
core.[0-9]*

# ── 4. PYTHON ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── 5. THIRD-PARTY SOURCE PAPERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copyrighted PDFs of the papers being reproduced. Not required to run anything;
# cite them instead. Generated reports under runs/ are tracked.
/15489_QueryStream_Advancing_St.pdf
/omnipro1.pdf

# ── 6. EDITOR / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
